  "generated_text": "To solve for \\(x\\) in the given system of linear equations:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n3x + 4y - 12z &= 10, \\tag{1} \\\\\n-2x - 3y + 9z &= -4, \\tag{2}\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nwe will use the method of elimination. First, we will eliminate \\(y\\) by making the coefficients of \\(y\\) in both equations equal in magnitude but opposite in sign.\n\n1. **Eliminate \\(y\\):**\n\n   Multiply equation (1) by 3 and equation (2) by 4 to make the coefficients of \\(y\\) equal in magnitude but opposite in sign:\n\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   3(3x + 4y - 12z) &= 3 \\cdot 10, \\\\\n   4(-2x - 3y + 9z) &= 4 \\cdot (-4).\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n   This gives us:\n\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   9x + 12y - 36z &= 30, \\tag{3} \\\\\n   -8x - 12y + 36z &= -16. \\tag{4}\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Add equations (3) and (4):**\n\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   (9x + 12y - 36z) + (-8x - 12y + 36z) &= 30 + (-16).\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n   Simplifying the left-hand side:\n\n   \\[\n   9x - 8x + 12y - 12y - 36z + 36z = 18x.\n   \\]\n\n   Simplifying the right-hand side:\n\n   \\[\n   30 - 16 = 14.\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, we have:\n\n   \\[\n   18x = 14.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Solve for \\(x\\):**\n\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{14}{18} = \\frac{7}{9}.\n   \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(x\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7}{9}}\\).",
